{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible","id":1365243,"title":"Why is resurrection impossible?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-04T06:51:14-08:00","id":1365243,"title":"Why is resurrection impossible?","content":"The out of game reason is obvious enough. But what about the in-game one? Everyone seems to treat it as fact. Wasn't death just one of the concepts invented by the primordials? <br /> <br /> On a related note, reincarnation itself IS a resurrection of sorts. It's even possible for a hun to remember some things from the life right before this one. In theory you could store someone's memories, trace his reincarnation and give them back to him. Depending on how much &quot;mojo&quot; you have, you may be able to recreate them just like that with whatever metaphysical explanation you can come with for your spell/artifact/etc<br /> <br /> I guess you could argue that this method might not restore that person's capabilities (and it definitely will not restore an exaltation), but it's still a resurrection for most intents and purposes<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T08:15:01-08:00","id":1365260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible#post1365243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The out of game reason is obvious enough. But what about the in-game one? Everyone seems to treat it as fact. Wasn't death just one of the concepts invented by the primordials?<br /> <br /> On a related note, reincarnation itself IS a resurrection of sorts. It's even possible for a hun to remember some things from the life right before this one. In theory you could store someone's memories, trace his reincarnation and give them back to him. Depending on how much &quot;mojo&quot; you have, you may be able to recreate them just like that with whatever metaphysical explanation you can come with for your spell/artifact/etc<br /> <br /> I guess you could argue that this method might not restore that person's capabilities (and it definitely will not restore an exaltation), but it's still a resurrection for most intents and purposes<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it is, but for some reason they will not live well their actual death, start being mad about it, and accept the pact of a Deathlord to become an Abyssal. <br /> <br /> It's a narrative rule addressed to the players and ST : death has a permanent narrative consequence, even if you can undo the physical consequence, the person will never be the same because she experienced something ineffable, that will affect her forever, for dramatic purpose. <br /> <br /> It's the same rule as &quot;Don't play a lazy character that stays in his sofa all adventure long doing nothing&quot; : Yeah there are some people like that, but don't play that story because it's boring (incoming stories about how people once had the best scenario ever with their lazy character staying all adventure in a sofa doing nothing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T08:17:05-08:00","id":1365261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible#post1365243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The out of game reason is obvious enough. But what about the in-game one? Everyone seems to treat it as fact. Wasn't death just one of the concepts invented by the primordials?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, it probably depends on how a given group thinks that level of the setting's cosmology works, if it's ever really able to turn up. My current leaning is towards the idea that &quot;inventing concepts&quot; might be a bit of a simplification for how one creates a universe.<br /> <br /> Regardless, that alone is not really making the case for the Exalted being able to do anything about it, since they don't have a whole lot that can do things to concepts as ontological qualities.<br /> <br /> As for why it can't be managed, I'm thinking of something analogous to the idea of dropping a crystal of salt into the ocean and then trying to recover and reconstruct that exact crystal precisely as it was after a period of time has passed in which you had to acquire any of the resources to do so; the total living being is something complex and needs all its parts in order to be whole and functional, and once it breaks down enough to no longer function independently some of the key components are going to become so dissolute that you'd never be able to grasp and recover all of them. Even if you could, in the time since they'd have all changed enough to not really be what they once were, and you'll never have the level of precise excision to get the wrong parts out.<br /> <br /> Not least because, are you sure you'd even know what was a change? Are you sure you <i>really</i> knew that person well enough?<br /> <br /> One can assert the existence of some form of magic that would automatically do all of that heavy lifting on your behalf, but another can easily veto it on the grounds that it's a huge reach and a cheat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a related note, reincarnation itself IS a resurrection of sorts. It's even possible for a hun to remember some things from the life right before this one. In theory you could store someone's memories, trace his reincarnation and give them back to him. Depending on how much &quot;mojo&quot; you have, you may be able to recreate them just like that with whatever metaphysical explanation you can come with for your spell/artifact/etc</div> </div> </div> </div>What <i>are</i> somebody's memories? A complete record of their life? Is it just what they remembered at the time of their death? But supposing the person died of old age and was pretty senile, how many memories do you want to recover for them? If you're using their memories from an earlier point of their life, are you really resurrecting the person that you knew? What if something important was in the memories that you left out? What if the person you knew was defined just as much by what they had forgotten as what they remembered?<br /> <br /> That's before even getting to the question of how much of identity is dependent on things that are not memory, that are not even conscious. If you have a favourite food, is it necessarily as a result of something present in memory? Was that also captured in the storage?<br /> <br /> And people are prone to remembering things inaccurately, even if those things had a profound impact on how their personality and views formed, perhaps especially so. You put in the way that the person remembered it, and you might very well get distinctly different results from the way that the person was actually shaped by it.<br /> <br /> Still, you're talking about loading memories into a separately existing person. If they've already formed their own personality and experiences, you're just getting a separate person loaded with another's memories. If you're doing it to a baby, well, babies can have more personality than you'd expect, and now you've got one that has a bunch of adult experiences without context or understanding pressed into their mushy little brain. Either way, you're not logically ending up with somebody even remotely resembling the one you want to bring back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's still a resurrection for most intents and purposes<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I did it; I brought my drinking buddy back! All can be forgiven for that punch in a drunken rage. Ah shit, it turns out that they're a real lightweight now on account of being several hundred pounds lighter and not having a fully developed metabolism. Hmm, nothing at all about this seems to recapture the relationship that I wanted to ensure didn't end for me.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T08:18:24-08:00","id":1365263,"title":"","content":"With the Liminals added to the setting, a simple reason why resurrection is impossible could be that the Dark Mother unfailingly hijacks all attempts at resurrection to create her Children of the Soil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T08:22:17-08:00","id":1365264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365263#post1365263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the Liminals added to the setting, a simple reason why resurrection is impossible could be that the Dark Mother unfailingly hijacks all attempts at resurrection to create her Children of the Soil.</div> </div> </div> </div>That the resurrection is a futile and desperate endeavour appears to be a key part of the mythology of the Chernozem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T09:01:53-08:00","id":1365270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible#post1365243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't death just one of the concepts invented by the primordials?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm of the opinion that this premise is something of a noose. Even if you don't care about the pre-history stuff Oblivion seems to have its own existence independent of anything the Primordials made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T09:10:11-08:00","id":1365272,"title":"","content":"Heck, I'd argue that the possibility of a permanent cessation to existence as an entity seems to be more of an emergent property of existence as an entity being meaningful, than something that was necessarily intentionally designed by any one being or beings.<br /> <br /> \u200b(And if your definition of resurrection is cast <i>so wide</i> that Exalted's model of reincarnation counts, then so does that Penny Arcade strip where Tycho, having accidentally killed his wife, <a href=\"https://www.penny-arcade.com/comic/2005/03/02/ripped-from-todays-headlines-pt.-5\" target=\"_blank\">paid twenty million dollars to a &quot;mad scientist&quot; to create a &quot;cybernetic replica&quot; of her.</a>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-04-2020, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T11:01:16-08:00","id":1365304,"title":"","content":"Exalted metaphysics also introduces degrees into the category of things that might be called resurrection.<br /> <br /> Are the Autochthonians more of a reincarnation of their previous lives because the Hun and Po are still joined? Is a person with the same higher soul and celestial exaltation more of a reincarnation of the former exalt than someone without the same higher soul?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T11:41:54-08:00","id":1365310,"title":"","content":"Is ressurection possible?<br /> <br /> In the Culture novels by Iain M. Banks, ressurection is a casual thing. The least peasant in the Culture can be restored to life, a perfect genetic copy with all their memories intact. No, more than that, the least peasant can just give that technology away to ressurect randos.<br /> <br /> But is that ressurection?<br /> <br /> It's Thesus' Paradox (explored as a sub-theme in Surface Detail, well worth a read).<br /> <br /> The same for ressurection in Exalted.<br /> <br /> What is life? What is death? What is ressurection?<br /> <br /> Can you step in the same river twice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T11:56:38-08:00","id":1365316,"title":"","content":"As a few others have pointed out how we're defining resurrection is probably important. Like I grab my buddies ghost and just have it possess a copy of his corpse that all the biological aspects functioning does that count? If I create an AI with a copy of all the person's memories and let it run loose have I brought them back? Does it only count if I use something like DnD's True Ressurection where you can call the person back from the afterlife so long as you have a severed limb or something to use as the basis for body reconstitution?*<br /> <br /> Now when the whole cycle of reincarnation thing is working properly then the easy answer is that there is no where to call the old soul back from even if you make the body functional again. The person died their soul reincarnated and has been scrubbed clean. Even if there are old memories or impressions that were missed putting the higher soul back in wouldn't have the old memories of their identity. If the person is a ghost, then I feel like it depends on that definition on whether or not possessing your own corpse counts as being brought back or not.<br /> <br /> As far as the Primordials inventing death goes my thoughts are that they designed how it works for Creation. Like in 2e its noted that Rhaksha could die all the time in the Wyld and would just shrug it off like it never happened. The whole part where dying in Creation or as a result of things from Creation (still 2e) was new to them. So it could be interpreted more as a scenario where as opposed to them inventing the idea that an entity can be ended, so much as making it a scenario where the end of an entity meant they stayed bloody ended and couldn't just pop up later with an &quot;I got better.&quot;<br /> <br /> *Huh, apparently 5e you don't even need the body parts anymore. Helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T12:21:58-08:00","id":1365325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365310#post1365310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the Culture novels by Iain M. Banks, ressurection is a casual thing. The least peasant in the Culture can be restored to life, a perfect genetic copy with all their memories intact. No, more than that, the least peasant can just give that technology away to ressurect randos.<br /> <br /> But is that ressurection?</div> </div> </div> </div>When I think about things like this, I find that they all go even simpler than Theseus' ship, depending on the answer to a single question:<br /> <br /> Is this a setting that integrates an apparent concept of a soul?<br /> <br /> If not, then no, it's not resurrection. Nothing you do well change the fact that the actual person in question experienced a cessation of consciousness from which there is no return.<br /> <br /> Still, a key subject in several narratives about the subject is who the resurrection is being done for the benefit of, the person whose life was lost or those they leave behind. There might well be people who are quite satisfied with this identical copy as a means of getting the list person back in their lives, but you've but really done the person that died a favour.<br /> <br /> ...Wait...<br /> <br /> {Levi, in a cosmology where there's no existence after death, do you not think that an instance of reviving life in the original brain and body of the lost person constitutes a return of life? If so, how is that functionally different from replicating those patterns otherwise? Doesn't a purely materialist world view become one in which the only meaningful definition of life is the instance of the person that is present and active?}<br /> <br /> Okay fine, I'll grant you that, but that still raises a question about the value and attachment that we place to the lives of others. It's hard not to feel as though that focus on a person as a material component has implications for how we conceive of and interact with people in general, alive or dead. There's something very transactional about it to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365316#post1365316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> *Huh, apparently 5e you don't even need the body parts anymore. Helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Surely that's how True Resurrection always worked? It goes Raise Dead for a fresh and fairly intact corpse, Resurrection for restoration from as little as a body part, True Resurrection for just springing them back from nothing. <br /> <br /> A cleric needs to be like, level 18 to learn that spell, don't they? Did Fifth Edition lower that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T12:37:31-08:00","id":1365328,"title":"","content":"Personally, I must admit that I'm rather unhappy with how resurrection (and, incidentally, time travel, and Yozi escaping to Creation) are handled in Exalted. The fact that they are simply impossible, period, seems to me just irritatingly heavy-handed, especially that reincarnation and weird time anomalies are a thing in Exalted.<br /> <br /> While I understand the reasons to remove these elements from the games as something casual, I really regret the rich body of tropes which are removed with them. Now, if you are desperately trying to bring back from dead your loved ones, you cannot make this struggle appropriately dramatic, since everyone at the table just know you will fail.<br /> <br /> I think it would be much better if the writers would simply leave this as a sidebar: &quot;Why you should avoid resurrection in your games and why this will never be a published spell&quot; and simply explain how DnD-esque spells would completely ruin the drama of death. But I definitely wouldn't remove plot-hookiness and rich context of that very trope (we houseruled that <i>potentially</i> resurrection and time travel could be a thing in the setting, but for all what we know in-game, they are impossible).<br /> <br /> Philosophical problems of continuity of self as an in-world justification for impossibility of resurrection seems a bit of a stretch here, since you could have them even in a setting with explicitly functional DnD-style resurrection.<br /> <br /> Notice, that you could pose analogous problems concerning continuity of, say, buildings (and the object-continuity problems are also discussed in philosophy in such contexts). Meanwhile, we have no sidebar saying &quot;no magic can bring a wooden chair to existence once it was burnt down, because how ontology works in the setting. However, you can reconstruct that chair perfectly.&quot; and indeed such a sidebar would be extremely awkward. I could imagine some deeply mythological justification for why resurrection could not happen (some Dark Mother or Oblivion involvement is an interesting suggestion though), but bringing in philosophy for justification of that fact seems nitpicking.<br /> <br /> I mean, philosophical discussion here is important and fascinating in real life, but used here seems rather irrelevant. The notion of causality is also discussed and yet no one sane would ever write in the book &quot;magic cannot cause object to move, since causality as a concept is fishy&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 02-04-2020, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T12:40:50-08:00","id":1365330,"title":"","content":"If I had to come up with an in-universe reason why resurrection is impossible, I'd say it's because the Celestials enforce the rules of mortality upon Creation as an immutable function of their very Essence.<br /> <br /> Alongside their geas to never harm the Primordials, the Celestials were also instilled with a geas to ensure that all denizens of Creation who aren't Primordial must not be able to recover from death and dissolution, to ensure the Primordials could get rid of their enemies permanently.<br /> <br /> Although the Primordials have been defeated, the Celestials can never stop obeying the rules the Primordials bound them by, and thus mortality will remain in Creation so long as there are gods in the firmament.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><i>Cue mad Circle of Exalts going on a quest to destroy all Celestials in order to defeat Death</i></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T13:01:40-08:00","id":1365333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365325#post1365325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Surely that's how True Resurrection always worked? It goes Raise Dead for a fresh and fairly intact corpse, Resurrection for restoration from as little as a body part, True Resurrection for just springing them back from nothing.<br /> <br /> A cleric needs to be like, level 18 to learn that spell, don't they? Did Fifth Edition lower that?</div> </div> </div> </div>17 according to my check. I don't know if that was always the thing, whenever it came up in my experience it was treated like you needed part of the body for it function. (To the extent of one group carrying around locks of eachother's hair in case the cause of death was fell into a volcano, disintegrate, or the like.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T13:11:04-08:00","id":1365334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365333#post1365333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if that was always the thing, whenever it came up in my experience it was treated like you needed part of the body for it function.</div> </div> </div> </div>True Resurrection has never, since D&amp;D 3e days, needed any body parts, just the name of the person. I believe True Res was introduced in 3e, but I don't know for certain, and it's possible it worked differently in earlier editions. But it's definitely been &quot;you don't need any part of the body&quot; since 3e.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T14:09:34-08:00","id":1365346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365328#post1365328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">especially that reincarnation and weird time anomalies are a thing in Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>People always bring up reincarnation as though there is a single real world religious system that acts as though it contains an assumption of personality continuity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, if you are desperately trying to bring back from dead your loved ones, you cannot make this struggle appropriately dramatic, since everyone at the table just know you will fail.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hadestown seemed to manage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T15:29:01-08:00","id":1365374,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365346#post1365346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hadestown seemed to manage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must admit that I don't quite understand the reference. Quick googling says that Hadestown was a musical based on the myth of Orpheus. I don't whether there is something particular about the musical, but I assume that you refer to the drama that can be present in the myth of Orpheus even though everyone know how it ends.<br /> <br /> I think this is indeed a deep question about how deeply specific role-playing games are as a medium. I could imagine a drama of a character trying to bring someone from dead fueled by dramatic irony: we know that this is futile and yet we try. Arguably, this is the drama you experience retelling the story of Orpheus.<br /> <br /> However, I think that the fundamental feature of rpg is that you retell the stories from the perspective of involved characters. Properly retelling a story of Orpheus in this particular medium would require you, to actually retell the hope that your journey to Hades can be successful, and then failing. I really think that <i>in roleplaying game</i> such an adaptation would be more true to the original story than bleak certainty that Eurydike will stay in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365346#post1365346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People always bring up reincarnation as though there is a single real world religious system that acts as though it contains an assumption of personality continuity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, ok. First we would have to make it clear how relevant to our discussion is continuity of common-sense personality as opposed to selfhood or personhood. I could imagine a nontrivial resurrection which changes personality. Indeed, it is the case in many stories depicting resurrection as an act of hubris. <br /> <br /> Second, at least some Greek philosophers (was it Plato?) made quasi-empirical case for reincarnation based on the anecdotes of people who apparently had memories that clearly belonged to recently deceased (everyday memories, not specifically Platonic <i>anamnesis</i>). <br /> <br /> Third, what is relevant here is how reincarnation functions in the setting of Exalted and it is explicitly allowed to alter reincarnation so that people retain their memories. I know, you mentioned personality, but the case should be made that this is impossible in Exalted. (If this impossible precisely because that would be resurrection then we go back to the question why this is more disruptive to the setting than retaining your memories.) <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T21:10:24-08:00","id":1365471,"title":"","content":"You can bring the dead back, but you can't resurrect them.<br /> <br /> That is, in bringing them back from the dead, they're no longer quite the same. Different body maybe. Different aspects to their character. Maybe now they're the same Hun but with a different Po. So there certainly are stories you can tell about venturing into the Underworld to retrieve your lover from death's embrace, but the end result will be different than &quot;casting true resurrection&quot;.<br /> <br /> I mean it doesn't have to be Pet Sematary, it could easily be Shadow of the Colossus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T23:35:40-08:00","id":1365488,"title":"","content":"I have always assumed that when the Primordials created Creation, they were limited by certain preconditions that made certain ways of creating Creation impossible, and certain ways possible; certain ways resource-intensive and certain ways resource-cheap; certain ways labor-intensive and certain ways easy.<br /> <br /> In much the same way that I, personally, here in the real world, could build a house any number of ways but could not build one that hovers in the air unsupported by anything, the Primordials could have made Creation any number of ways but could <i>not</i> just make it any way they pleased with no limits to how they did it or what the final outcome was. And Creation and everything in it works the way it does because of the set of choices they made before the dawn of time, between <i>this</i> way things could have been and another way things could have been that they decided against because, given the bounded number of choices available to them, this was the one they thought suited their purposes and resources best.<br /> <br /> So, in that respect, death probably works the way it does and not some other way not because &quot;death as it <i>does</i> work&quot; just happens to be the concept as they envisioned it, but rather because in order for it to work a different way they would have had to make tradeoffs they didn't want to make.<br /> <br /> (I'm not at all interested in exploring what those initial boundary conditions were, though. Something something mumble shinma.)<br /> <br /> You might as well ask &quot;Why quarks?&quot; or &quot;Why the higgs-boson?&quot; There's probably a reason and it's probably even interesting but it's probably not going to be existentially fulfilling, and will probably boil down to &quot;Because math has to work this way for things to be self-consistent.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 02-05-2020, 02:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T23:51:22-08:00","id":1365490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365325#post1365325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I think about things like this, I find that they all go even simpler than Theseus' ship, depending on the answer to a single question:<br /> <br /> Is this a setting that integrates an apparent concept of a soul?<br /> <br /> If not, then no, it's not resurrection. Nothing you do well change the fact that the actual person in question experienced a cessation of consciousness from which there is no return.<br /> <br /> Still, a key subject in several narratives about the subject is who the resurrection is being done for the benefit of, the person whose life was lost or those they leave behind. There might well be people who are quite satisfied with this identical copy as a means of getting the list person back in their lives, but you've but really done the person that died a favour.<br /> <br /> ...Wait...<br /> <br /> {Levi, in a cosmology where there's no existence after death, do you not think that an instance of reviving life in the original brain and body of the lost person constitutes a return of life? If so, how is that functionally different from replicating those patterns otherwise? Doesn't a purely materialist world view become one in which the only meaningful definition of life is the instance of the person that is present and active?}<br /> <br /> Okay fine, I'll grant you that, but that still raises a question about the value and attachment that we place to the lives of others. It's hard not to feel as though that focus on a person as a material component has implications for how we conceive of and interact with people in general, alive or dead. There's something very transactional about it to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You assume that, in the absence of the soul or an afterlife, a perfect copy isn't a resurrection because the person in question &quot;experienced a cessation of consciousness from which there is no return,&quot; but you have to admit that <i>from the subjective point of view of the copy</i>, there was no cessation -- the original isn't around, and from the copy's point of view they are the original because it's all just memories. So, followup question: If the cessation of consciousness that we call sleep, or even the cessation of consciousness that we call <i>losing our train of thought</i>, were equivalent to death, and we're all just copies of ourselves walking around inside our own heads <i>already</i>...<br /> <br /> ...would we have any way of knowing?<br /> <br /> And what would that mean for resurrection via perfect copies?<br /> <br /> (The concept of the self is socially constructed; because we are educated on our worldview and perspective by our peers and the social norms they teach us. Destructive teleporters would catch on within less than a lifetime because some people would use them, and then everyone else would be powerfully incentivized to see the teleporter-copies/copy-resurrections as the originals, and then peer pressure would take take care of everything else and soon enough the socially constructed version of identity we all use would include the-copy-is-the-original. Except for a few holdouts, who\u2019d quickly become disenfranchised from the global economy.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 02-05-2020, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-05T03:30:31-08:00","id":1365513,"title":"","content":"If you crack an egg, you can scoop up the yolk and white, put it back in the shell and tape the shell closed again. You've kind of &quot;un-cracked&quot; it, but the marks are still there. It's obviously not back to it's original state.<br /> <br /> Shoving a soul back in the body and reanimating it is probably the same. Sure, you can make someone <i>functionally </i>&quot;alive&quot; again but it's not gonna be seamless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-05T14:39:56-08:00","id":1365612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible#post1365243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The out of game reason is obvious enough. But what about the in-game one? Everyone seems to treat it as fact. Wasn't death just one of the concepts invented by the primordials?<br /> <br /> On a related note, reincarnation itself IS a resurrection of sorts. It's even possible for a hun to remember some things from the life right before this one. In theory you could store someone's memories, trace his reincarnation and give them back to him. Depending on how much &quot;mojo&quot; you have, you may be able to recreate them just like that with whatever metaphysical explanation you can come with for your spell/artifact/etc<br /> <br /> I guess you could argue that this method might not restore that person's capabilities (and it definitely will not restore an exaltation), but it's still a resurrection for most intents and purposes<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You could restore a human being with a cloned body and recycled soul, they just have the ambiguous they are different and not exactly the same tag.<br /> <br /> Similarly someone can die, become a ghost, the ghost becomes a god and the God is changed into a mortal, they are not quite the same but they are technically the same entity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T09:14:02-08:00","id":1365741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365261#post1365261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What <i>are</i> somebody's memories? A complete record of their life? Is it just what they remembered at the time of their death? But supposing the person died of old age and was pretty senile, how many memories do you want to recover for them? If you're using their memories from an earlier point of their life, are you really resurrecting the person that you knew? What if something important was in the memories that you left out? What if the person you knew was defined just as much by what they had forgotten as what they remembered?<br /> <br /> That's before even getting to the question of how much of identity is dependent on things that are not memory, that are not even conscious. If you have a favourite food, is it necessarily as a result of something present in memory? Was that also captured in the storage?<br /> <br /> And people are prone to remembering things inaccurately, even if those things had a profound impact on how their personality and views formed, perhaps especially so. You put in the way that the person remembered it, and you might very well get distinctly different results from the way that the person was actually shaped by it.<br /> <br /> Still, you're talking about loading memories into a separately existing person. If they've already formed their own personality and experiences, you're just getting a separate person loaded with another's memories. If you're doing it to a baby, well, babies can have more personality than you'd expect, and now you've got one that has a bunch of adult experiences without context or understanding pressed into their mushy little brain. Either way, you're not logically ending up with somebody even remotely resembling the one you want to bring back.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;I did it; I brought my drinking buddy back! All can be forgiven for that punch in a drunken rage. Ah shit, it turns out that they're a real lightweight now on account of being several hundred pounds lighter and not having a fully developed metabolism. Hmm, nothing at all about this seems to recapture the relationship that I wanted to ensure didn't end for me.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>When i mentioned tracking someone's reincarnation i meant doing so LONG before developing a new personality is an issue. Such <br /> 1. i cast a spell to find out where his new life is. Maybe i need something that belonged to him or whatever<br /> 2. I physically age him to an adult form Or move his soul using magic(necromancy is ideal) or whatever. Babies' personality is like a drop of honey in an ocean. Notice how the Ebon dragon is kinda scared that actual mature infernals(talking about second edition here) might suffer a bit of a personality crisis due to him not deleting the exaltation's memories. At any rate, let's say i format the baby's mind and soul just to be on the safe side.<br /> 3.I restore his memories using whatever method suits me. Maybe he had stored most of his memories in an artifact. Maybe he had an artifact that continuously fed new memories to a central material intelligence. Maybe i just reverse the process of Lethe. Think of how, if you have a plastic surgery done, the scar will give any surgeon a pretty accurate image of how your face must have looked before. With the help of magic this image becomes completely accurate. Think of it like a laser done backwards if it makes sense. Or maybe i look past in time to capture his memories. Or i invoke the idea of that person's memories. Ok, metaphysics can get a little fuzzy, but you get the idea.<br /> <br /> Honestly, lethe seems heavy-handed to me. It resurrects people...but deletes their memories and personalities. Except for people who do keep a few of their past life memories. According to the past life background anyway(Honestly, i did not like that book at all)<br /> <br /> But if we define resurrection as &quot;reattaching a soul to a body normally(i.e no need to constantly feed it with essence or having it rot away etc)&quot; Lethe is a resurrection<br /> This begs the question : Is the mind wipe actually necessary or was is simply something decided by the primordials and that some 9 person committee of gods and exalts decided to keep in the year 3 of the primordial defeat, as part of heavenly law 321b-2?<br /> <br /> I just hate things for which there is no metaphysical explanation other than &quot; accept it&quot; Again, i understand why the no resurrection rule is dramatically appropriate from an out of game perspective<br /> , but it seems impossible for me to come up with an equally good in-game explanation<br /> Especially because, as i mentioned, it's a rule with a huge loophole","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T09:29:59-08:00","id":1365747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365488#post1365488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have always assumed that when the Primordials created Creation, they were limited by certain preconditions that made certain ways of creating Creation impossible, and certain ways possible; certain ways resource-intensive and certain ways resource-cheap; certain ways labor-intensive and certain ways easy.<br /> <br /> In much the same way that I, personally, here in the real world, could build a house any number of ways but could not build one that hovers in the air unsupported by anything, the Primordials could have made Creation any number of ways but could <i>not</i> just make it any way they pleased with no limits to how they did it or what the final outcome was. And Creation and everything in it works the way it does because of the set of choices they made before the dawn of time, between <i>this</i> way things could have been and another way things could have been that they decided against because, given the bounded number of choices available to them, this was the one they thought suited their purposes and resources best.<br /> <br /> So, in that respect, death probably works the way it does and not some other way not because &quot;death as it <i>does</i> work&quot; just happens to be the concept as they envisioned it, but rather because in order for it to work a different way they would have had to make tradeoffs they didn't want to make.<br /> <br /> (I'm not at all interested in exploring what those initial boundary conditions were, though. Something something mumble shinma.)<br /> <br /> You might as well ask &quot;Why quarks?&quot; or &quot;Why the higgs-boson?&quot; There's probably a reason and it's probably even interesting but it's probably not going to be existentially fulfilling, and will probably boil down to &quot;Because math has to work this way for things to be self-consistent.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry, for the double post, i missed the fact that there was a second page.<br /> <br /> Ok, that sort of makes sense i guess, except for the fact that it does not explain how Lethe is special. If i had to guess, i'd say that what the primordials got in return was that they could influence reality in a greater way, under that system. As can their successors. Maybe this is why Exalted has a loom of fate while the wod doesn't. Maybe that's how the incarna managed to metaphysically make time travel illegal. But i'm navel gazing lol<br /> <br /> Going back to the issue at hand, it might help explain my reasoning if i bring a dungeons and dragons example<br /> <br /> Imagine we are in a 3.5 edition game. I create an epic spell that works out like true resurrection except for the following<br /> <br /> The target of the spell becomes a baby. <br /> <br /> He loses all his memories permanently and inherently (meaning break enchantment ain't gonna fix anything)<br /> <br /> He loses his subconscious too. (alingment, sense of humor, levels, stuff like that)<br /> <br /> But it's still a resurrection. His soul is recalled from where ever it was. <br /> I know that the concept of self is a complex philosophical issue, but he is still the same person in the sense that he still experiences things through his own eyes. The lights never go out etc<br /> <br /> <br /> My point here is, that in many games such a thing would actually be a more powerful spell than a traditional resurrection.. though i have seen examples of the opposite admittedly . Depends on your perspective of &quot;power&quot;<br /> This i can understand with your explanation, but what still bugs me is whether, under such conditions my original idea would work ( Restoring memories to an infant, which you have magically aged so long as we ignore the concept of &quot;self&quot; in the same way that Ligier suffering fetich death is still supposed to be his &quot;self&quot; when he comes back as the red star&quot; Just for the purpose of ignoring a philosophical debate with no obvious answer<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T09:30:46-08:00","id":1365748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365741#post1365741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But <b>if </b>we define resurrection as &quot;reattaching a soul to a body normally(i.e no need to constantly feed it with essence or having it rot away etc)&quot; Lethe is a resurrection</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br /> <br /> But what if we define resurrection like, you know, the way people who use the regular definition do?<br /> <br /> \u200b&quot;Resurrection, the state of one risen from the dead.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bSince it's not the same <i>entire</i> soul, into a body that doesn't look the same, and doesn't have access to even a sizable portion of the original's memories, it's pretty clear that the reincarnation process in Creation is not something that fits in the standard definition of &quot;resurrection,&quot; and if the end result of your shoehorning it into a category with a special definition makes you uncomfortable with it, why not just <i>not do that</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-06-2020, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T10:42:50-08:00","id":1365763,"title":"","content":"1st and 2nd Edition Alchemicals both had Soul Archiving Protocol, allowing you to put a ghost into a soulgem, and then into a new Alchemical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T11:01:21-08:00","id":1365765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365747#post1365747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sorry, for the double post, i missed the fact that there was a second page.<br /> <br /> Ok, that sort of makes sense i guess, except for the fact that it does not explain how Lethe is special. If i had to guess, i'd say that what the primordials got in return was that they could influence reality in a greater way, under that system. As can their successors. Maybe this is why Exalted has a loom of fate while the wod doesn't. Maybe that's how the incarna managed to metaphysically make time travel illegal. But i'm navel gazing lol<br /> <br /> Going back to the issue at hand, it might help explain my reasoning if i bring a dungeons and dragons example<br /> <br /> Imagine we are in a 3.5 edition game. I create an epic spell that works out like true resurrection except for the following<br /> <br /> The target of the spell becomes a baby.<br /> <br /> He loses all his memories permanently and inherently (meaning break enchantment ain't gonna fix anything)<br /> <br /> He loses his subconscious too. (alingment, sense of humor, levels, stuff like that)<br /> <br /> But it's still a resurrection. His soul is recalled from where ever it was.<br /> I know that the concept of self is a complex philosophical issue, but he is still the same person in the sense that he still experiences things through his own eyes. The lights never go out etc<br /> <br /> <br /> My point here is, that in many games such a thing would actually be a more powerful spell than a traditional resurrection.. though i have seen examples of the opposite admittedly . Depends on your perspective of &quot;power&quot;<br /> This i can understand with your explanation, but what still bugs me is whether, under such conditions my original idea would work ( Restoring memories to an infant, which you have magically aged so long as we ignore the concept of &quot;self&quot; in the same way that Ligier suffering fetich death is still supposed to be his &quot;self&quot; when he comes back as the red star&quot; Just for the purpose of ignoring a philosophical debate with no obvious answer<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect there is a rather large bit of metaphysical infrastructure tucked away somewhere, that took a tremendous amount of effort to create, that runs Lethe. The game hardly ever spells out what the Well of Souls is (there's a 2e book that says it's the sky, but that sort of comes out of nowhere and doesn't really mean anything), but I think it's probably part of it. I think breaking it would be a bad idea.<br /> <br /> (Which is another way of saying: Maybe you could resurrect someone &quot;properly&quot; if you could go back in time and harness the power of all of the Primordials at their full strength and had them build a tremendous occult machine the size of Heaven to do it, and then tucked it away into a fold in space-time so nobody could see it. As of RY 768 this is...probably... not a thing you can do.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 02-06-2020, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T11:30:42-08:00","id":1365778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365765#post1365765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suspect there is a rather large bit of metaphysical infrastructure tucked away somewhere, that took a tremendous amount of effort to create, that runs Lethe. The game hardly ever spells out what the Well of Souls is (there's a 2e book that says it's the sky, but that sort of comes out of nowhere and doesn't really mean anything), but I think it's probably part of it. I think breaking it would be a bad idea.<br /> <br /> (Which is another way of saying: Maybe you could resurrect someone &quot;properly&quot; if you could go back in time and harness the power of all of the Primordials at their full strength and had them build a tremendous occult machine the size of Heaven to do it, and then tucked it away into a fold in space-time so nobody could see it. As of RY 768 this is...probably... not a thing you can do.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can think of other potential ways. Doing something a shinmaic calibration to alter the universe. Along with that miracle-shell mechanism. Change the universe. Essentially remove true resurrection from the Beyond. Alternatively travel to an alternative universe where the primordials created a different creation. Introduce legislation to Yu-shan that makes time warping possible again. In this scenario you can make a spell which says&quot; John's death never happened&quot; All easier said than done of course Find the prime 9 archmage that made creation and ask him to change things! Ok , i was joking about the last one(a bit)<br /> <br /> <br /> On a related note, it just hit me. Is tracing someone's reincarnation actually possible?* It's conceivable that as part of the &quot;no resurrection rule&quot; , it's impossible for anyone, save for the maiden of secrets and an awakened sachaverell to know such a thing, making the restoration of memories scheme impossible. Or at least as unlikely as winning the federal lottery <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T12:05:03-08:00","id":1365795,"title":"","content":"I've often been a bit confused by the Sinmaic Calibration charm, are there really any limits to it? It seems to me like the First Age should have been WAY crazier as it's written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T12:47:40-08:00","id":1365811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365795#post1365795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've often been a bit confused by the Sinmaic Calibration charm, are there really any limits to it? It seems to me like the First Age should have been WAY crazier as it's written.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure it required the tech from the Cauldron Project. Which I think most of us remember as the-proposed-plan-to-unmake-reality-and-wyldshape-a-new-one. The proposal and growing popularity of which was one of the major reasons that led to the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> So I would guess the limits aren't there because its supposed to be remaking reality from the ground up hence no limitations, and why it didn't end up doing more in the First Age was because it never happened back then.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T14:11:52-08:00","id":1365837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365778#post1365778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a related note, it just hit me. Is tracing someone's reincarnation actually possible?* It's conceivable that as part of the &amp;quot;no resurrection rule&amp;quot; , it's impossible for anyone, save for the maiden of secrets and an awakened sachaverell to know such a thing, making the restoration of memories scheme impossible. Or at least as unlikely as winning the federal lottery <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Authochthonia does it as a matter of course, and is allow for magic of a similar form to their soul gems to not be very difficult (even if producing and implementing it at that scale is).<br /> <br /> Although... that one is not merely a matter of power but logistics. It's not just that everybody's soul is marked, but that the marks are archived and there's an institution to examine every newborn infant to determine their last life. So you could put something on a soul to recognise it, but actually finding it afterwards...<br /> <br /> Technically possible, but on its own difficult to the point of impossible. So I guess it needs to be a mark that you can detect from range.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I feel as though there are plausibly divinations that could find that information, but that they're fairly powerful and the knowledge of them is rare.<br /> <br /> Efficient Secretary Technique might be capable of it, depending on how it's written this time. The First Edition and pre-errata Second Edition versions certainly could.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365795#post1365795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've often been a bit confused by the Sinmaic Calibration charm, are there really any limits to it? It seems to me like the First Age should have been WAY crazier as it's written.</div> </div> </div> </div>The crazier you make it the higher the successes needed to realize it, and anything bigger than a single Wyld-shaped region requires lots of additional shenanigans to be undertaken. The Salinan Working required rituals across all of Creation and resources sanctioned by the Deliberative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T14:26:28-08:00","id":1365840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365837#post1365837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Authochthonia does it as a matter of course, and is allow for magic of a similar form to their soul gems to not be very difficult (even if producing and implementing it at that scale is).<br /> <br /> Although... that one is not merely a matter of power but logistics. It's not just that everybody's soul is marked, but that the marks are archived and there's an institution to examine every newborn infant to determine their last life. So you could put something on a soul to recognise it, but actually finding it afterwards...<br /> <br /> Technically possible, but on its own difficult to the point of impossible. So I guess it needs to be a mark that you can detect from range.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I feel as though there are plausibly divinations that could find that information, but that they're fairly powerful and the knowledge of them is rare.<br /> <br /> Efficient Secretary Technique might be capable of it, depending on how it's written this time. The First Edition and pre-errata Second Edition versions certainly could.<br /> <br /> <br /> The crazier you make it the higher the successes needed to realize it, and anything bigger than a single Wyld-shaped region requires lots of additional shenanigans to be undertaken. The Salinan Working required rituals across all of Creation and resources sanctioned by the Deliberative.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If i am not mistaken Autochthonia requires or citizens to have a gen on their bodies that swallows their souls when they die??<br /> <br /> Speaking of which... autochthonia has some lethe substitute, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T15:01:52-08:00","id":1365853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365840#post1365840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If i am not mistaken Autochthonia requires or citizens to have a gen on their bodies that swallows their souls when they die??<br /> <br /> Speaking of which... autochthonia has some lethe substitute, right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> All Autochthonians who live in the Eight Nations have a soul gem implanted in their forehead just after they're born. Upon death, the soul gem captures and makes a mark on the soul about its life and deeds. It's then standard, as part of the funeral rites, to release the soul. Autochthon does have an equivalent to Lethe, which scrubs the soul's memories, but not the record created by the soul gem. When a child is born, specialists in the Eight Nations can read their soul and, using the record from previous incarnations, assign it to a suitable caste in Autochthonian society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T15:23:26-08:00","id":1365857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365811#post1365811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure it required the tech from the Cauldron Project. Which I think most of us remember as the-proposed-plan-to-unmake-reality-and-wyldshape-a-new-one. The proposal and growing popularity of which was one of the major reasons that led to the Usurpation.</div> </div> </div> </div>It looks to me the way it's printed it just works if you have the charm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365837#post1365837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The crazier you make it the higher the successes needed to realize it, and anything bigger than a single Wyld-shaped region requires lots of additional shenanigans to be undertaken. The Salinan Working required rituals across all of Creation and resources sanctioned by the Deliberative.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, but the highest difficulty you get on that extended roll is 5, which affects &quot;All of existence, even those conceptual frontiers the Exalted have yet to discover or invent.&quot;. Past that the biggest cumulative difficulty you get is 210, if you want a single trigger. At which point you're affecting all people everywhere in existence, regardless of how powerful they are, with an effect equivalent to Adamant Circle Sorcery, until the end of time.<br /> <br /> If you have the stats that Bright Shattered Ice or Salina have in that book, that's well doable in less than a month of work. Could Bright Shattered Ice just be like &quot;I don't like all these gods and other exalted messing around, I'm going to make a Shinmaic calibration that triggers whenever anyone except me uses a charm of a certain power or more (pick an essence, say 3) instead it burns their essence out, dealing damage and lowering their permanent essence score by 1.&quot; Then suddenly every god, demon, exalt, whatever anywhere except Bright Shattered Ice gets handcuffed, forever, since any charm that could undo that Shinma would trigger the effect and you'd be unable to.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's a pretty extreme example, but there's lots you could do anyway. Creation should be boingo-boingo-whoopsie-knickers-bonkerz after a few Twilights shuffle around reality like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T15:49:05-08:00","id":1365865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365853#post1365853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">All Autochthonians who live in the Eight Nations have a soul gem implanted in their forehead just after they're born. Upon death, the soul gem captures and makes a mark on the soul about its life and deeds.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The most comprehensive information about soulgems was in Ink Monkeys<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, which stated that the mark itself contains no actual information other than its own identification. It's basically a barcode, unique to each instance in which it's used but you have to independently place the information designating what it refers to into a database.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Which is to say that the Luminors still need to maintain extensive archives about soul lineages (helped by the Olgotory's general level of observation and record keeping) to make decisions. It is said outright that they need to consult archives of personal profiles and soul legacies, external to the mark left on the soul.<br /> <br /> One might infer from this that making a soul retain comprehensive information about its own life is a bit more of an investment. </span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365857#post1365857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It looks to me the way it's printed it just works if you have the charm.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be overlooking the very important final paragraphs of the Charm. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Charm's miracles take effect automatically once crafting is complete, unless the Solar has utilized one or more points of Nirupadhika. In that case the miracle becomes what is known as a shinmaic potentiality or &quot;Miracle Shell&quot;, an Essence-shaped working which exists in potential but does not interface with Creation. Greater arts than Shinmaic Calibration are required to integrate a Miracle Shell into reality - the Salinan Working is likely the most well-known example of such a working. </div> </div> </div>To remind again, since you... ignored it completely, the Salinan Working (one described as only consisting of seventeen points) required rituals conducted all around the world to be conducted in addition to resources provided by (and general legal sanction from) the Solar Deliberative to put it into reality. It would be reasonable to assume that your proposed 21 point Miracle Shell would require even more dramatic efforts. Putting no points into Nirupadhika means that the thing can only have the scope of a single Wyld-shaped region.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T15:56:38-08:00","id":1365868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365865#post1365865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To remind again, since you... ignored it completely, the Salinan Working (one described as only consisting of seventeen points) required rituals conducted all around the world to be conducted in addition to resources provided by (and general legal sanction from) the Solar Deliberative to put it into reality. It would be reasonable to assume that your proposed 21 point Miracle Shell would require even more dramatic efforts. Putting no points into Nirupadhika means that the thing can only have the scope of a single Wyld-shaped region.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I was reading it wrong, I thought it was saying the effects don't take place unless the Solar has used Nirupadhika. So basically it's just &quot;This charm lets you completely rewrite reality however you want, as long as your put as much effort as your Storyteller deems appropriate for that task.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T16:11:40-08:00","id":1365877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365865#post1365865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to be overlooking the very important final paragraphs of the Charm. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Putting no points into Nirupadhika means that the thing can only have the scope of a single Wyld-shaped region.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, that's a new level of bad editing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T16:13:28-08:00","id":1365878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365868#post1365868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes I was reading it wrong, I thought it was saying the effects don't take place unless the Solar has used Nirupadhika. So basically it's just &quot;This charm lets you completely rewrite reality however you want, as long as your put as much effort as your Storyteller deems appropriate for that task.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Why didn't the Solars of the 2e First Age make Creation really really really gonzo wacky?&quot;<br /> Because each of them wanted to make Creation into their own personal Magical Ream and the other 299 Solars were like &quot;that's not my fetish&quot; and shot it down, so only the most inoffensive global shifts [or deceptively written ones, such as perhaps the Salinan Working, which might well have been the *reason* they all sat up and went 'uh let's not let this happen again'] or local-scaled weirdness were authorized and had adequate resources and permissions dedicated to them. XP<br /> <br /> Hey look, &quot;as much effort as the Storyteller deems appropriate&quot; leads to a perfectly adequate reason things are 99% indistinguishable from the normal world in outcome if not cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T16:15:21-08:00","id":1365879,"title":"","content":"And for that level of effort you too can have a played as originally written Void Avatar Prana and Zeal combo!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T16:20:59-08:00","id":1365881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365878#post1365878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey look, &quot;as much effort as the Storyteller deems appropriate&quot; leads to a perfectly adequate reason things are 99% indistinguishable from the normal world in outcome if not cause.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you can see how, by misreading that final paragraph, it would seem to have a massive disconnect between the setting and the charm. With a Twilight just sitting in her basement for a few weeks remaking all the laws of reality such that even Primordials and Incarna can't resist them. You'd expect the world to be a lot weirder if that was the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T16:24:31-08:00","id":1365882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365879#post1365879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And for that level of effort you too can have a played as originally written Void Avatar Prana and Zeal combo!</div> </div> </div> </div>Enlighten me to these horrors of which you speak. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T16:32:08-08:00","id":1365884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365877#post1365877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow, that's a new level of bad editing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I beg your pardon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T16:48:51-08:00","id":1365890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365882#post1365882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Enlighten me to these horrors of which you speak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Void Avatar Prana was the capstone to the Abyssal martial arts style in 2e, and due to ambiguous wording, many took it to basically be scene-length access to a one-mote perfect defense.<br /> <br /> \u200bZeal, on the other hand, was a <i>Dreams of the First Age</i> Integrity Charm that let a Solar spend a Virtue channel to overcome a perfect defense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-06-2020, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T16:53:07-08:00","id":1365893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365884#post1365884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I beg your pardon?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that it's really difficult to notice that this charm is just a variation of Wyld Shaping Technique, which <i>potentially</i> allows you to affect non-Wyld-shaped regions if the Storyteller agrees. The way it's written looks almost intentionally confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T17:28:50-08:00","id":1365898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365893#post1365893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean that it's really difficult to notice that this charm is just a variation of Wyld Shaping Technique, which <i>potentially</i> allows you to affect non-Wyld-shaped regions if the Storyteller agrees.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it is. Shinmaic Calibration has a prerequisite Charm, its less talked about, less sexy cousin Shinmaic Communion, which states that it can only be used in a region that the Solar created via Wyld-shaping, and had Wyld Cauldron Technology as a prerequisite. Shinmaic Calibration states in its own first paragraph that it can only be activated in a region that has been altered with Communion. Aaaannnd the first two levels of Nirupadhika state that they only affect regions that the Solar has Wyld-shaped; you need three points of that to affect the rest of Creation at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way it's written looks almost intentionally confusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way it's written means that for First Age or otherwise high Essence games, there's a compromise by which people can achieve dramatic effects without the entire world being at stake, and there are so many reminders of that for when the text is actually read rather than talked about in discussions that gravitate so quickly to the most overwhelming applications of power.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ohhh, now I get it.<br /> <br /> So another limitation behind DrLoveMonkey's scenario is that the Solar in question needs to have purchased Shinmaic Communion six times in order to have the twenty two points necessary to sink into the region before it can even serve as the foundation of a Miracle Shell with that level of power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 02-06-2020, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T09:15:31-08:00","id":1366043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365741#post1365741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if we define resurrection as &quot;reattaching a soul to a body normally(i.e no need to constantly feed it with essence or having it rot away etc)&quot; Lethe is a resurrection</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, if you define it that way, it is. So if you don't actually care if the result is in a different body, has a different lower soul, and doesn't retain their memories, &quot;resurrection&quot; is possible.<br /> <br /> So, the key problem in resurrection, as usually understood, is not putting the hun in a new body. It's that you cannot create a being that has proper continuity of personality/identity with the person who died, even if you have continuity of memory.<br /> <br /> If you're looking for an obvious metaphysical root of the issue, then, it's probably the po, which is intimately linked to both the body and hun. The trauma of death presumably changes the po in some way, such that if you try to reunite body, po, and hun, you get a different personality. Your sorcery can glue the pieces back together, but it's still not the same pot; it's got a spiderweb pattern of cracks filled with sorcery-adhesive. You can alternatively forge a new po to link body and soul, but you again get a new personality, because the po, and thus the soul of the new being, is not the same as the original's, in particular because it didn't grow with the body. Stuffing a recording of old memories into a reincarnated person definitely doesn't work, because this time the body and po are both different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T15:58:12-08:00","id":1366142,"title":"","content":"Oh! Note that the inability to resurrect now also is of a piece with other limits on undoing with sorcery:<br /> <br /> &quot;Once a spell has been cast, its effects cannot be undone, but a skilled sorcerer may mute, twist, or weaken them with a distort action.&quot; Page 466.<br /> <br /> &quot;The closest thing to dispelling a working that a rival sorcerer can do is performing a working of her own intended to achieve the opposite effect.&quot; Page 489.<br /> <br /> So the same metaphysical &quot;entropy&quot; or &quot;inertia&quot; or suchlike explains why you can't undo death. You can approximate resurrection like you can approximate undoing sorcery, but there's ultimately an irreconcilable gap; things do not go back to the way they were before, you effort creates a third state instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T03:21:59-08:00","id":1366278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1365865#post1365865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most comprehensive information about soulgems was in Ink Monkeys<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, which stated that the mark itself contains no actual information other than its own identification. It's basically a barcode, unique to each instance in which it's used but you have to independently place the information designating what it refers to into a database.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Which is to say that the Luminors still need to maintain extensive archives about soul lineages (helped by the Olgotory's general level of observation and record keeping) to make decisions. It is said outright that they need to consult archives of personal profiles and soul legacies, external to the mark left on the soul.<br /> <br /> One might infer from this that making a soul retain comprehensive information about its own life is a bit more of an investment. </span></span></span></div><br /> <br /> <br /> You seem to be overlooking the very important final paragraphs of the Charm. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> To remind again, since you... ignored it completely, the Salinan Working (one described as only consisting of seventeen points) required rituals conducted all around the world to be conducted in addition to resources provided by (and general legal sanction from) the Solar Deliberative to put it into reality. It would be reasonable to assume that your proposed 21 point Miracle Shell would require even more dramatic efforts. Putting no points into Nirupadhika means that the thing can only have the scope of a single Wyld-shaped region.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Does the mark disappear upon reincarnation? In other words if my next life does not have a soulgem will it still have a barcode once i am born again?<br /> <br /> I had forgotten much about the soulgems. I almost wish they did not exist just so the &quot; return someone's memories to him once they reincarnated&quot; loophole that i thought became a non-issue. But as it stands out, i see no easy way out of it. .<br /> I like what someone said that your personality depends in part on your po but even if you can't arrange for an identical po to joined with the hun in question, it will still leave the individual mostly similar to the one who came before . To put it in freudian terms, the only part of your mind that would be different is the lower one(i think Freud called it ID but i am not sure)<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of shinmaic cummunation, i never quite understood what the miracle shell does. Mostly because the actual charm does not exist, but is implied to be at essence 8","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T09:13:42-08:00","id":1366338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366278#post1366278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the mark disappear upon reincarnation? In other words if my next life does not have a soulgem will it still have a barcode once i am born again?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't disappear on reincarnation, but on death. The mark is still there to be identified on the newborn before they're given a soul gem, but they need that soul gem to be sure that they'll have a new mark for the next life. Note also that part of the reason to capture the soul is to give the Luminors the opportunity to record the new mark; it would be useless to mark a soul if you didn't know what it looked like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had forgotten much about the soulgems. I almost wish they did not exist just so the &amp;quot; return someone's memories to him once they reincarnated&amp;quot; loophole that i thought became a non-issue. But as it stands out, i see no easy way out of it. .</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you think a baby suddenly given the memories of a full lifetime will be like? Will they at all resemble the dead person?<br /> <br /> One thing I always found interesting about the Dragon Kings was that while they had a form of reincarnation that allowed access to all the previous lifetime's memories and thus had an expectation that you were a continuation of that life, there were acknowledgements that this was a cultural construct rather than something completely accurate. With the fact that full access to those memories only came with higher Essence, it was recognised that there would be time for an individual to form their own personality and aspirations before they ever felt much like the last person, so it never really was a case of people simply resurrecting perpetually, even if their society acted as though it was.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like what someone said that your personality depends in part on your po but even if you can't arrange for an identical po to joined with the hun in question, it will still leave the individual mostly similar to the one who came before . To put it in freudian terms, the only part of your mind that would be different is the lower one(i think Freud called it ID but i am not sure)</div> </div> </div> </div>Suppose I reincarnate the soul of an ancient Roman person, even with the capacity to develop accurate memories of that life, in the body of a lifelong inhabitant of, let's say, San Francisco. Is the end result likely to be identical to the original Roman? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of shinmaic cummunation, i never quite understood what the miracle shell does. Mostly because the actual charm does not exist, but is implied to be at essence 8</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't do anything, it just exists until you do a bunch of things like Salina did to implant it in reality. <br /> <br /> Shinmaic Calibration was an interesting attempt to represent the Salinan Working as an elder power while still being reconciled with those things I said before about not totally overwhelming the setting, but it's still very apparent that it's cobbled together post hoc and not an entirely smooth fit. It relies a bit on the reader to not pick at the gaps too much.<br /> <br /> Workings as a basic power of sorcery from the outset is ultimately more functional, and accessible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T12:53:07-08:00","id":1366383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366278#post1366278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like what someone said that your personality depends in part on your po but even if you can't arrange for an identical po to joined with the hun in question, it will still leave the individual mostly similar to the one who came before . To put it in freudian terms, the only part of your mind that would be different is the lower one(i think Freud called it ID but i am not sure)</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of pretty fundamental stuff happens there, though. The Freudian id covers bodily needs, wants, desires, and impulses. A replacement <i>po</i> in Creation might well swap them from being attracted to tall, leggy women to being attracted to short, round men, with all the resulting dissonance with memories of what they used to be attracted to thrown in. And even lesser changes can be disconcerting; I recall at this point Esri Dax in <i>Star Trek: Deep Space Nine</i> ordering raktajino even though she doesn't like it, because previous lives liked it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T13:27:02-08:00","id":1366389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366142#post1366142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh! Note that the inability to resurrect now also is of a piece with other limits on undoing with sorcery:<br /> <br /> &quot;Once a spell has been cast, its effects cannot be undone, but a skilled sorcerer may mute, twist, or weaken them with a distort action.&quot; Page 466.<br /> <br /> &quot;The closest thing to dispelling a working that a rival sorcerer can do is performing a working of her own intended to achieve the opposite effect.&quot; Page 489.<br /> <br /> So the same metaphysical &quot;entropy&quot; or &quot;inertia&quot; or suchlike explains why you can't undo death. You can approximate resurrection like you can approximate undoing sorcery, but there's ultimately an irreconcilable gap; things do not go back to the way they were before, you effort creates a third state instead.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's interesting that the world itself can return, not to the same state but to a similar one, by just waiting for a spell's duration to end. Even theoretically permanent sorcerous workings and artifacts can fail over time. Of course this is just another manifestation of entropy. Probably related is the fact that even the longest-lived exalts can still die.<br /> <br /> It would be interesting, though, to discover that something about Creation that we think is completely normal is in fact the result of some epic First Age Sorcery that, though distorted, was never completely removed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T14:16:25-08:00","id":1366397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366389#post1366389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's interesting that the world itself can return, not to the same state but to a similar one, by just waiting for a spell's duration to end. Even theoretically permanent sorcerous workings and artifacts can fail over time. Of course this is just another manifestation of entropy. Probably related is the fact that even the longest-lived exalts can still die.<br /> <br /> It would be interesting, though, to discover that something about Creation that we think is completely normal is in fact the result of some epic First Age Sorcery that, though distorted, was never completely removed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think sorcerous workings &quot;fail over time&quot;. They just change or become apparently useless, because their initial conditions is no more. To me, sorcery is about making a definitive change to the world. The problem is rather that some permanent changes are tied to a condition to &quot;function well&quot; (being fed magical energy, having a cult maintain it, etc ...). If I wanted to make a comparison, suppose someone finds a phone in a future where there is no more electricity. This is still a phone, even though it doesn't do anything, it does not regress to just be a huge piece of carbon, cobalt and lithium and stuff smashed together. (You could also destroy the phone, but at this point the phone is not &quot;failing&quot;, it is just no more)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T14:23:26-08:00","id":1366398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366389#post1366389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's interesting that the world itself can return, not to the same state but to a similar one, by just waiting for a spell's duration to end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if you wait out a casting of Death of Obsidian Butterflies, the ground over which the spell was cast will not be safe to walk on. The glass butterflies don't just poof.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T16:07:15-08:00","id":1366421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366397#post1366397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think sorcerous workings &quot;fail over time&quot;. They just change or become apparently useless, because their initial conditions is no more. To me, sorcery is about making a definitive change to the world. The problem is rather that some permanent changes are tied to a condition to &quot;function well&quot; (being fed magical energy, having a cult maintain it, etc ...). If I wanted to make a comparison, suppose someone finds a phone in a future where there is no more electricity. This is still a phone, even though it doesn't do anything, it does not regress to just be a huge piece of carbon, cobalt and lithium and stuff smashed together. (You could also destroy the phone, but at this point the phone is not &quot;failing&quot;, it is just no more)</div> </div> </div> </div>Then are there tons of dormant sorcerous workings around anywhere?<br /> <br /> What if the area the sorcerous working was in is absorbed by the Wyld, then you Wyldshape a new stable territory around it?<br /> <br /> I do agree with the phone metaphor. It won't just stop being a phone, but it could run out of electricity / some magical resource, it could develop inexplicable bugs and quirks, and (I think, though I am not completely certain - forgive me for being a bit argumentative when I'm trying to learn) it could be destroyed and end up as dust. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366398#post1366398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if you wait out a casting of Death of Obsidian Butterflies, the ground over which the spell was cast will not be safe to walk on. The glass butterflies don't just poof.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but they will shatter and degrade into sand at the same rate as ordinary glass. Or else the whole world would be covered in black butterflies from past sorcerers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-08T16:34:25-08:00","id":1366428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366421#post1366421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then are there tons of dormant sorcerous workings around anywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say so, yeah. A lot of them probably aren't even &quot;dormant&quot;, in the sense of no longer having an effect. Their effects are either just so minuscule and diffuse that they're hard to notice, or else they've just become part of people's everyday lives to the point that nobody realizes that things haven't always been that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the area the sorcerous working was in is absorbed by the Wyld, then you Wyldshape a new stable territory around it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how the original working was done, I would say. If the working specifically affected the material of Creation (a fertility ritual that made the soil more capable of sustaining life, for example), then it is probably gone, effectively, since the original material was lost. If it more changed an area of space, though (a fertility ritual that gave extra Wood essence to all plants within a certain range), that might still apply. But it could well have moved from its original location, since distance and space gets funky in the Wyld, and in any case, detecting that it was there might be tricky. All of this, though, definitely sounds like some good fodder for declaring facts via Lore. I'd allow a player who was about to engage in a big Wyld-shaping project to declare a fact with Lore that one of the areas she wanted to shape was already under a fertility-enhancing working, for instance.<br /> <br /> I do agree with the phone metaphor. It won't just stop being a phone, but it could run out of electricity / some magical resource, it could develop inexplicable bugs and quirks, and (I think, though I am not completely certain - forgive me for being a bit argumentative when I'm trying to learn) it could be destroyed and end up as dust.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but they will shatter and degrade into sand at the same rate as ordinary glass. Or else the whole world would be covered in black butterflies from past sorcerers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the point, though, is that there is always <i>something</i> around from any sorcery that wasn't there before. The obsidian butterflies might not stay in that exact form, but Creation now has more obsidian shards, sand, or whatever than it did before, because the spell was cast. Sorcery always makes a permanent change to the world, even if the <i>directed</i> effects of the spell end after a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T13:52:16-08:00","id":1366624,"title":"","content":"I'm going to attempt to thread the needle and assert that sorcery and sorcerous workings are permanent but not indelible. The changes wrought by sorcery don't poof, and getting rid of one is never as easy as just flipping the magic back off, but, as they are real, they can be acted upon by outside forces just like any other real thing.<br /> <br /> Note, however, also, that sorcerous workings aren't just, <i>or even primarily</i> meant to model &quot;Local persistent change to the laws of physics.&quot; Their original source of inspiration was &quot;How do we model stuff like Mazirian the Magician from Jack Vance's <i>Dying Earth</i> trying to create homonculi-people by growing progressively better ones in vats; he's clearly <i>doing magical stuff</i> but he's definitely <i>not</i> researching a spell that, once he knows it, he'll be able to spam to create more and more homonculi. What if we had some sort of system for one-off magical effects that let you do more freeform stuff than spells let you do, but which you have to basically research anew every time?&quot; The sample sorcerous working in the corebook is just making a walking hut. Presumably you can start hitting it with your sword, at which point the ST has to make up some combat stats for it, and then if you win the fight you have a broken walking hut and a dead animating spirit that's no longer animating anything because it's dead.<br /> <br /> There's even rules for getting your XP back if your working is ever completely nullified. It just, you know, has to be nullified by addressing what it does, and not by casting dispel magic. Which kinda returns us to the original question -- there's no resurrection magic because undoing stuff that's been done is never as easy as casting an undo spell. You can do <i>something like</i> undo, by binding a ghost into a homonculous and maybe even doing magical brain surgery on its hungry ghost and then stitching them back together or something, but you'll have to address all the problems as you find them, many of them won't be perfectly surmountable, and all the means you use to solve the problem are themselves real and create further change. No takeback; no matter how much you want to return things to an earlier state, you can only push them into further new ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 02-09-2020, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T14:02:49-08:00","id":1366627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366624#post1366624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note, however, also, that sorcerous workings aren't just, <i>or even primarily</i> meant to model &quot;Local persistent change to the laws of physics.&quot; Their original source of inspiration was &quot;How do we model stuff like Mazirian the Magician from Jack Vance's <i>Dying Earth</i> trying to create homonculi-people by growing progressively better ones in vats; he's clearly <i>doing magical stuff</i> but he's definitely <i>not</i> researching a spell that, once he knows it, he'll be able to spam to create more and more homonculi. What if we had some sort of system for one-off magical effects that let you do more freeform stuff than spells let you do, but which you have to basically research anew every time?&quot; </div> </div> </div> </div>Let me just chime in to say that your attempt was extremely. successful. Sorcerous workings are one of my favourite pieces of mechanics across all roleplaying games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T14:08:42-08:00","id":1366631,"title":"","content":"Note that the no-takebacks thing is the original sin of the Primordials -- &quot;before&quot; Creation, time wasn't linear, and for the entities of the Wyld it was possible to go forward and backwards and sideways, and if you killed someone you could un-kill them and if you died it was possible to just un-die and if you made a change to your existence you didn't like you could unmake it, and if something changed about your relationship to another entity you could un-change it, and then the Primordials made Creation and now <i>no matter how far into the Wyld you go</i>, the linear arrow of time is 100% inescapable and you can't have do-overs for your messy breakups. It is probably not possible for entities such as us, used to dwelling within linear time, to fully conceptualize such an existence, but nevertheless that's the way things were before the dawn of time. Many of the unshaped Wyld entities who want to break Creation believe that by doing so, they can undo time and return to that Edenic (for-them) state, and they may not be wrong for wanting this, because the Primordials sure didn't ask them for permission before making this change.<br /> <br /> (It's kinda too bad for them that in order to assume enough shape to be able to meaningfully interact with Creation in a way that might allow them to break it, they have to pass through the gateway of Sundraprisha and bind themselves to things like form and time and identity, which leaves them in a state where what they've become will as surely be destroyed by Creation's breaking as any native of the world the Primordials made.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T17:29:23-08:00","id":1366663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366631#post1366631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that the no-takebacks thing is the original sin of the Primordials -- &quot;before&quot; Creation, time wasn't linear, and for the entities of the Wyld it was possible to go forward and backwards and sideways, and if you killed someone you could un-kill them and if you died it was possible to just un-die and if you made a change to your existence you didn't like you could unmake it, and if something changed about your relationship to another entity you could un-change it, and then the Primordials made Creation and now <i>no matter how far into the Wyld you go</i>, the linear arrow of time is 100% inescapable and you can't have do-overs for your messy breakups. It is probably not possible for entities such as us, used to dwelling within linear time, to fully conceptualize such an existence, but nevertheless that's the way things were before the dawn of time. Many of the unshaped Wyld entities who want to break Creation believe that by doing so, they can undo time and return to that Edenic (for-them) state, and they may not be wrong for wanting this, because the Primordials sure didn't ask them for permission before making this change.<br /> <br /> (It's kinda too bad for them that in order to assume enough shape to be able to meaningfully interact with Creation in a way that might allow them to break it, they have to pass through the gateway of Sundraprisha and bind themselves to things like form and time and identity, which leaves them in a state where what they've become will as surely be destroyed by Creation's breaking as any native of the world the Primordials made.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I was always under the impression that primordials carried their own linearity. That is, if they killed a raksha in pre-creation time, it stayed dead. After all the primordials were always static linear beings. Autochthon was always the inventor. Theion was always the King etc<br /> <br /> I do believe that(in the previous editions) time travel is possible. Books talk about how time magic was used during the primordial war. It is something that changed after the war. For whatever reason. To this day the yozis can declare that an event that happened in hell within the last 5 days never happened.<br /> <br /> The way i imagine pre-creation existence is ,ironically, a lot like the eponymous Ascension from mage the Ascension. Actions having no consequence, everyone having his own reality, no real need to interact with others. Until the primordials emerged.<br /> <br /> By the way, this edenic state is still supposed to apply in some cases. If a raksha kills a raksha in the wyld, it is nothing but a dream to be willed away.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T17:57:53-08:00","id":1366668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366663#post1366663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way i imagine pre-creation existence is ,ironically, a lot like the eponymous Ascension from mage the Ascension. Actions having no consequence, everyone having his own reality, no real need to interact with others. Until the primordials emerged.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!<br /> <br /> You just gave me a brilliant idea for future Wod vs Exalted stories...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T18:31:45-08:00","id":1366673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366663#post1366663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is, if they killed a raksha in pre-creation time, it stayed dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Were there raksha in pre-Creation?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366663#post1366663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After all the primordials were always static linear beings.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Were</i> they?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366663#post1366663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Autochthon was always the inventor. Theion was always the King etc</div> </div> </div> </div>If Theion was always the king, what of Mardukth, the Mountain and the Beast Upon It?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366663#post1366663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do believe that(in the previous editions) time travel is possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>don't </i>believe that, in previous editions, going backward through time was possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366663#post1366663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Books talk about how time magic was used during the primordial war.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time-dilation can be a thing without necessarily being able to visit the past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366663#post1366663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To this day the yozis can declare that an event that happened in hell within the last 5 days never happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not <i>quite</i>. In 2e and only 2e, an Exalt could ask a Yozi to reshape <i>Hell </i>to <i>effectively </i>undo some event that had happened there in the last five days. So if I killed Gervesin in the Demon City right before a sorcerer in Creation had planned to summon him, and then a day after the attempted summoning fails, ask Malfeas to restore Gervesin to life, the sorcerer's summoning spell <i>will still have failed</i>. New!Gervesin won't just be shaped into existence chilling on the sorcerer's couch.<br /> <br /> \u200bMore importantly, it's not something that got carried over into 3e, so saying &quot;to this day&quot; they can do it, isn't accurate either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T01:19:01-08:00","id":1366711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366663#post1366663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was always under the impression that primordials carried their own linearity. That is, if they killed a raksha in pre-creation time, it stayed dead. After all the primordials were always static linear beings. Autochthon was always the inventor. Theion was always the King etc</div> </div> </div> </div>In the same way that a Rhaksha might carry its own internalized view of how events have transpired, maybe but 2e covered it the most and even if mentioned that Rhaksha with a more linear view of time tend to be ones that have come in contact with Creation and those that have managed to avoid it are under no such restriction. It also doesn't help that the utter madness of the of the Deep Wylds ,absent Creation it is all you'd have, the only way to differentiate a linear path would be one's own interpretation of events or maybe one forced upon you by another entity.<br /> <br /> As far as Primordial titles go, I'll give that they may have been what they were but that's less them being linear beings and more that 2e played them as more sentient concepts. Malfeas and his proto form were the king because they were a concept of king as was Mardukth also the king because he was a different concept of king. Also Oramus will always screw with that considering his origin in 2e was coming into existence after the other Primoridials to greet them and express how it had started getting worried they were never going to arrive/wake up with how long it had been waiting. Meaning Oramus predated itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366663#post1366663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do believe that(in the previous editions) time travel is possible. Books talk about how time magic was used during the primordial war. It is something that changed after the war. For whatever reason. To this day the yozis can declare that an event that happened in hell within the last 5 days never happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>First the measure was under half an hour (possibly significantly, but its late and I don't want to look through the books for specifics) not almost a week, and that was openly declared a case of not true just ignore it by the devs of the time. It has certainly not been carried over into 3rd.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T02:54:32-08:00","id":1366722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366673#post1366673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Were there raksha in pre-Creation?<br /> <br /> <i>Were</i> they?<br /> <br /> If Theion was always the king, what of Mardukth, the Mountain and the Beast Upon It?<br /> <br /> I <i>don't </i>believe that, in previous editions, going backward through time was possible.<br /> <br /> Time-dilation can be a thing without necessarily being able to visit the past.<br /> <br /> Not <i>quite</i>. In 2e and only 2e, an Exalt could ask a Yozi to reshape <i>Hell </i>to <i>effectively </i>undo some event that had happened there in the last five days. So if I killed Gervesin in the Demon City right before a sorcerer in Creation had planned to summon him, and then a day after the attempted summoning fails, ask Malfeas to restore Gervesin to life, the sorcerer's summoning spell <i>will still have failed</i>. New!Gervesin won't just be shaped into existence chilling on the sorcerer's couch.<br /> <br /> \u200bMore importantly, it's not something that got carried over into 3e, so saying &quot;to this day&quot; they can do it, isn't accurate either.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry, by Raksha i meant the unshaped<br /> Theion was always the king in the sense that he always embodied kingship/authority Metaphysically. He did not always have this role because he happened to wake up far away from his brethren<br /> No, previous books were explicit. Such as &quot;primordial x died between the first week and the 180 year of the war because extensive use of time magic makes coherent records impossible.<br /> When i said &quot;to this day&quot; I meant in-game not out of game. I was not aware that this got retconned to be honest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366338#post1366338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't disappear on reincarnation, but on death. The mark is still there to be identified on the newborn before they're given a soul gem, but they need that soul gem to be sure that they'll have a new mark for the next life. Note also that part of the reason to capture the soul is to give the Luminors the opportunity to record the new mark; it would be useless to mark a soul if you didn't know what it looked like.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What do you think a baby suddenly given the memories of a full lifetime will be like? Will they at all resemble the dead person?<br /> <br /> One thing I always found interesting about the Dragon Kings was that while they had a form of reincarnation that allowed access to all the previous lifetime's memories and thus had an expectation that you were a continuation of that life, there were acknowledgements that this was a cultural construct rather than something completely accurate. With the fact that full access to those memories only came with higher Essence, it was recognised that there would be time for an individual to form their own personality and aspirations before they ever felt much like the last person, so it never really was a case of people simply resurrecting perpetually, even if their society acted as though it was.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Suppose I reincarnate the soul of an ancient Roman person, even with the capacity to develop accurate memories of that life, in the body of a lifelong inhabitant of, let's say, San Francisco. Is the end result likely to be identical to the original Roman?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It doesn't do anything, it just exists until you do a bunch of things like Salina did to implant it in reality.<br /> <br /> Shinmaic Calibration was an interesting attempt to represent the Salinan Working as an elder power while still being reconciled with those things I said before about not totally overwhelming the setting, but it's still very apparent that it's cobbled together post hoc and not an entirely smooth fit. It relies a bit on the reader to not pick at the gaps too much.<br /> <br /> Workings as a basic power of sorcery from the outset is ultimately more functional, and accessible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, dragon king memories come back with higher essence. But what if you forcibly gave a human his full memories back upon birth. Of course i have no idea what would happen, neurologically, to a baby if this were to occur. Or for that matter a baby that had its body magically aged to adulthood, but was still a baby in terms of having 0 experiences.<br /> <br /> Memory is most explicitly NOT the same as aptitude after all... and a baby has none. Would it suffer a psychosis? Permanent insanity?<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that in Exalted giving someone an aptitude(such as an ability) seems to be very difficult, but i'll have to relook the specific charms again.<br /> <br /> <br /> Concerning shinmaic communation, upon reading the charms i get the impression that<br /> the charm is completely useless without shinmaic calibration. It only does cosmetic effects<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","user":"mark","date":". 02-10-2020, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T06:29:16-08:00","id":1366756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366722#post1366722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, previous books were explicit. Such as &amp;quot;primordial x died between the first week and the 180 year of the war because extensive use of time magic makes coherent records impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is easily a consequence of time dilation, and arguably makes far more sense for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed; you're not resurrecting somebody, you're making a new person that is weird.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Concerning shinmaic communation, upon reading the charms i get the impression that<br /> the charm is completely useless without shinmaic calibration. It only does cosmetic effects</div> </div> </div> </div>The lowest form of Nirupadhika makes it impossible to get lost or to go anywhere other than a specific destination, the middle form can reduce travel times by half or more (I know I'd like to make hour long bus trips in ten minutes), the highest forms make a landmass that can be mobile or bigger on the inside.<br /> <br /> Dharma makes residing in the territory alter a person's Intimacies.<br /> <br /> Nirvishesha gives it Wyld qualities, an abundance of a particular kind of spirit, or control over the soul cycle.<br /> <br /> Low levels of Nishkriya make the populace more deeply inclined towards the Solar's wars, high levels make a landscape that will naturally act to assault any of their enemies that enter.<br /> <br /> And Nirvikalpa controls its mundane or mystical natural resources.<br /> <br /> Those are not purely cosmetic effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T07:48:11-08:00","id":1366777,"title":"","content":"Note that most of the lore about pre--war Primordials -- Mardukth, Theion, etc. -- came well after <i>Exalted: The Fair Folk</i> established Creation's creation as an event horizon after which time became fixed, and was made up by people who weren't even freelancers yet when E:tFF was written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T11:55:21-08:00","id":1366822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366756#post1366756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is easily a consequence of time dilation, and arguably makes far more sense for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Indeed; you're not resurrecting somebody, you're making a new person that is weird.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The lowest form of Nirupadhika makes it impossible to get lost or to go anywhere other than a specific destination, the middle form can reduce travel times by half or more (I know I'd like to make hour long bus trips in ten minutes), the highest forms make a landmass that can be mobile or bigger on the inside.<br /> <br /> Dharma makes residing in the territory alter a person's Intimacies.<br /> <br /> Nirvishesha gives it Wyld qualities, an abundance of a particular kind of spirit, or control over the soul cycle.<br /> <br /> Low levels of Nishkriya make the populace more deeply inclined towards the Solar's wars, high levels make a landscape that will naturally act to assault any of their enemies that enter.<br /> <br /> And Nirvikalpa controls its mundane or mystical natural resources.<br /> <br /> Those are not purely cosmetic effects.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm, i guess we can just agree to disagree about that one. I know it would not technically be a resurrection, but if done very correctly i would view it as one for all practical intents and purposes<br /> Except for the fact that the created person would not have the same stats as the old one. E.g an ancient solar's intelligence 8 might become intelligence 5. His charisma 3 may become charisma 1-2. Maybe pushed a little more with various training effects but even they have a limit.<br /> So it's not a resurrection in the sense that you can not play the same character sheet i guess.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, i've been reading shinmaic communion and calibration and they seem ... weird<br /> <br /> shinmaic communion says : five points tithed to nishkriya turn the region into a weapon against enemies who suffer one environmental attack per hour. This seems great but..<br /> <br /> Shinmaic calibration: The parameters of the effect depend on the shinmaic communion affecting the region<br /> <br /> Nirviklakpa determines the power of the miracle : zero points limits the effects to only the weakest happenstance effects with no mechanical repercussions<br /> <br /> These two seem contradictory. Should i take this to imply that shinmaic communion does some general stuff while calibration does something more specific?<br /> <br /> For example, under calibration the salinan working Nirupadhika 5 Nirvishesha 5 Dharma 4 Nishkriya 1 Nirvikalpa 2 Plus the greater powers needed for Nirupadhika 1+ effects<br /> <br /> So, in order to do this, would i also need some speficic Shinmaic Communion effects???<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366777#post1366777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that most of the lore about pre--war Primordials -- Mardukth, Theion, etc. -- came well after <i>Exalted: The Fair Folk</i> established Creation's creation as an event horizon after which time became fixed, and was made up by people who weren't even freelancers yet when E:tFF was written.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I suppose you could see that lore as allegorical, trying to explain pre-linear time to beings who never lived under it<br /> Still, do i get the impression that many exalted writers just never read the previous works or communicated with each other? Uhm, no offense meant to you personally<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","user":"mark","date":". 02-10-2020, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T13:06:14-08:00","id":1366838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366822#post1366822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> These two seem contradictory. Should i take this to imply that shinmaic communion does some general stuff while calibration does something more specific?</div> </div> </div> </div>Shinmaic Communion only does what each level says on the tin. Shinmaic Calibration can go bigger and have more precision, but how far each of its parameters can go is dependent on the seed territory. <br /> <br /> If you commune with the shinma to alter a place without so much as improvement to its forests and farmland, then you can't calibrate the shinma to do any more than create particular visual effects. If you commune to create a demesne, you can calibrate to make anything up to miracles akin to the most powerful sorcery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, under calibration the salinan working Nirupadhika 5 Nirvishesha 5 Dharma 4 Nishkriya 1 Nirvikalpa 2 Plus the greater powers needed for Nirupadhika 1+ effects<br /> <br /> So, in order to do this, would i also need some speficic Shinmaic Communion effects???</div> </div> </div> </div>In the starting territory, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, do i get the impression that many exalted writers just never read the previous works or communicated with each other?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much.<br /> <br /> Exalted writers are freelancers. We've got freelancers who have a personal dedication to the line and are more invested in all of its elements, and ones for whom it's just another job. The latter does not make them bad writers, probably some of the best stuff in the game has been produced by some of them, but it puts the onus for book consistency more on the developer for the book and line.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> [/QUOTE]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T19:33:29-08:00","id":1366908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366838#post1366838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but it puts the onus for book consistency more on the developer for the book and line.</div> </div> </div> </div>And, for 2nd edition from the start through Return of the Scarlet Empress, I don't think its continuity was well-served on the line level.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T07:04:39-08:00","id":1366966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366822#post1366822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, do i get the impression that many exalted writers just never read the previous works or communicated with each other?</div> </div> </div> </div> That's not even the worst of it, there's writers who were in little edit wars with each other.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T07:13:48-08:00","id":1366968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366624#post1366624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to attempt to thread the needle and assert that sorcery and sorcerous workings are permanent but not indelible. The changes wrought by sorcery don't poof, and getting rid of one is never as easy as just flipping the magic back off, but, as they are real, they can be acted upon by outside forces just like any other real thing.<br /> <br /> Note, however, also, that sorcerous workings aren't just, <i>or even primarily</i> meant to model &quot;Local persistent change to the laws of physics.&quot; Their original source of inspiration was &quot;How do we model stuff like Mazirian the Magician from Jack Vance's <i>Dying Earth</i> trying to create homonculi-people by growing progressively better ones in vats; he's clearly <i>doing magical stuff</i> but he's definitely <i>not</i> researching a spell that, once he knows it, he'll be able to spam to create more and more homonculi. What if we had some sort of system for one-off magical effects that let you do more freeform stuff than spells let you do, but which you have to basically research anew every time?&quot; The sample sorcerous working in the corebook is just making a walking hut. Presumably you can start hitting it with your sword, at which point the ST has to make up some combat stats for it, and then if you win the fight you have a broken walking hut and a dead animating spirit that's no longer animating anything because it's dead.<br /> <br /> There's even rules for getting your XP back if your working is ever completely nullified. It just, you know, has to be nullified by addressing what it does, and not by casting dispel magic. Which kinda returns us to the original question -- there's no resurrection magic because undoing stuff that's been done is never as easy as casting an undo spell. You can do <i>something like</i> undo, by binding a ghost into a homonculous and maybe even doing magical brain surgery on its hungry ghost and then stitching them back together or something, but you'll have to address all the problems as you find them, many of them won't be perfectly surmountable, and all the means you use to solve the problem are themselves real and create further change. No takeback; no matter how much you want to return things to an earlier state, you can only push them into further new ones.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Perhaps(going back to the set of choices the primordials made) this also explains why even healing magic is difficult in that setting. Relative to others anyway.<br /> <br /> This raises an interesting question. Are the primordials themselves capable of re-engineering the universe NOW? Or does yozification permanently remove that capability? Many books imply that their surrender mutilations reduced their power to create and do the impossible<br /> <br /> Or maybe the solar deliberative, at the height of its power, could do such a thing, if they were prepared for the consequences.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366966#post1366966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's not even the worst of it, there's writers who were in little edit wars with each other.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I thought gamelines usually have some central director(s) or something. Someone to draw some lines in the sand. Or for that matter someone to look into the finished product and remove a few lines, instead of declaring them non canon later in a forum that people years later might not have access too.<br /> <br /> Cause i sure as hell did not see any such thing in scrolls of errata or ink monkeys.<br /> <br /> Not to mention someone to look at early drafts<br /> <br /> Am i the only one who thinks the mechanics of scroll of heroes are bad lol ?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","user":"mark","date":". 02-11-2020, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T08:34:43-08:00","id":1366986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366968#post1366968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought gamelines usually have some central director(s) or something. Someone to draw some lines in the sand. Or for that matter someone to look into the finished product and remove a few lines, instead of declaring them non canon later in a forum that people years later might not have access too.</div> </div> </div> </div>They should, but sometimes the oversight of more limited, and even at the best of times there can be discrepancies that aren't with getting hung up over.<br /> <br /> There's also a matter of adhering to deadlines that can make having a writer do something over impractical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cause i sure as hell did not see any such thing in scrolls of errata or ink monkeys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that wasn't really the function of either of those things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T11:32:44-08:00","id":1367044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366968#post1366968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am i the only one who thinks the mechanics of scroll of heroes are bad lol ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The writer of the God-Blooded chapter came on to the WW forums when the book was released, and, well, the experience wasn't pleasant for him.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T12:14:37-08:00","id":1367056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1367044#post1367044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The writer of the God-Blooded chapter came on to the WW forums when the book was released, and, well, the experience wasn't pleasant for him.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really sad actually","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T13:35:57-08:00","id":1367079,"title":"","content":"It's not a sequence of events I'd allow to repeat no matter how bad the writing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T08:04:43-08:00","id":1367539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1367044#post1367044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The writer of the God-Blooded chapter came on to the WW forums when the book was released, and, well, the experience wasn't pleasant for him.</div> </div> </div> </div>A small but vocal part of Exalted's fanbase seems to be rather toxic...to say the least. I heard that back in the day some writer's had their lives threatened<br /> <br /> Writing a horrible chapter(and it was indeed atrocious in terms of mechanics) does not even come close to justifying such behavior","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T08:45:54-08:00","id":1367542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366968#post1366968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This raises an interesting question. Are the primordials themselves capable of re-engineering the universe NOW? Or does yozification permanently remove that capability? Many books imply that their surrender mutilations reduced their power to create and do the impossible</div> </div> </div> </div>It's real hard to re-engineer the universe when you're trapped in Hell, forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T16:47:36-08:00","id":1367645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1367539#post1367539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A small but vocal part of Exalted's fanbase seems to be rather toxic...to say the least. I heard that back in the day some writer's had their lives threatened</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we're talking about something from more than ten years ago. I don't think every single member of the White Wolf forum community of the time participated in such activity, but I'd say the board culture of way back when was not what it is now, and outright harassment was more the far end of a spectrum than a few isolated bad actors.<br /> <br /> And while this board and a couple of others moved on from that approach*, I've caught passing glimpses from some others in which that kind of attitude continues to thrive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Writing a horrible chapter(and it was indeed atrocious in terms of mechanics) does not even come close to justifying such behavior</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that you mean well, but also feel it's necessary to point out the issue of a wording that implies that there are ever circumstances in which harassment is okay. That's not on you, it's a shortcoming of particular uses of the language, and perhaps an enduring problem of a society averse to considering problems systemically.<br /> <br /> Which brings me back to the point that there was once a forum culture that bred hostility that could verge into harassment.<br /> <br /> * At least by my assessment. Last I saw, there was still an attitude that this forum was extremely insular and hostile to contrary opinions, but I'm not sure whether or not to take that as a perspective that would change were it looked at now or one made in bad faith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T17:17:51-08:00","id":1367651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1367539#post1367539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(and it was indeed atrocious in terms of mechanics)</div> </div> </div> </div>You're telling the guy who wrote and publicly released a complete replacement PDF for those rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5