 class=\"message\">It's real hard to re-engineer the universe when you're trapped in Hell, forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>right right. I meant in a hypothetical event in which the Yozis were free. In a sense, whether or not the Yozis's somewhat deranged plan can work is irrelevant. They believe it can and act accordingly. So, if they COULD re-engineed the world as mutilated but free Yozis it would allow for a deeper alliance with the Neverborn. Their end goals need no longer be contradictory<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1367645#post1367645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, we're talking about something from more than ten years ago. I don't think every single member of the White Wolf forum community of the time participated in such activity, but I'd say the board culture of way back when was not what it is now, and outright harassment was more the far end of a spectrum than a few isolated bad actors.<br /> <br /> And while this board and a couple of others moved on from that approach*, I've caught passing glimpses from some others in which that kind of attitude continues to thrive.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I know that you mean well, but also feel it's necessary to point out the issue of a wording that implies that there are ever circumstances in which harassment is okay. That's not on you, it's a shortcoming of particular uses of the language, and perhaps an enduring problem of a society averse to considering problems systemically.<br /> <br /> Which brings me back to the point that there was once a forum culture that bred hostility that could verge into harassment.<br /> <br /> * At least by my assessment. Last I saw, there was still an attitude that this forum was extremely insular and hostile to contrary opinions, but I'm not sure whether or not to take that as a perspective that would change were it looked at now or one made in bad faith.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, i should have clarified what i meant .Anyway, Harassment, bullying/etc are absolutely NOT ok under any circumstances<br /> <br /> I think what i had in mind when writing &quot;does not even come close&quot; was a court yelling at a self- proclaimed mass murderer in his trial or something like that. In the sense that people yelling in that scenario would not really be the bad guys But that scenario would not be &quot;harassment&quot; though, so bad choice of words on my part<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","user":"mark","date":". 02-21-2020, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T03:19:32-08:00","id":1369314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1369304#post1369304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can these still be found online by the way? Assuming it was a free pdf i mean</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't find it anywhere, or I'd have linked it. (I can find a site that alleges to have it, but it just has a dead link.)<br /> <br /> My local copy was lost in a computer transfer long ago (the one that led to my current multiply-redundant backup system), and I guess I figured it was safe on my webserver and didn't download a local copy (and so apparently lost it in the failure of my webhosting company and transfer of my site to a new one). I do have my <i>first</i> release of <i>Annals of Inherited Might</i> still, but that was the version that wasn't bugfixed by forum discussion. Maybe someone here on the forums still has a copy of the fixed version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T04:57:19-08:00","id":1369332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1369314#post1369314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't find it anywhere, or I'd have linked it. (I can find a site that alleges to have it, but it just has a dead link.)<br /> <br /> My local copy was lost in a computer transfer long ago (the one that led to my current multiply-redundant backup system), and I guess I figured it was safe on my webserver and didn't download a local copy (and so apparently lost it in the failure of my webhosting company and transfer of my site to a new one). I do have my <i>first</i> release of <i>Annals of Inherited Might</i> still, but that was the version that wasn't bugfixed by forum discussion. Maybe someone here on the forums still has a copy of the fixed version.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would still appreciate having that, if the bugfixed version is unavailable.<br /> <br /> Isn't this the sort of thing that would be included in the scroll of errata anyway?<br /> <br /> Personally i always portrayed half-splats in a way similar to the Lintha","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T10:55:55-07:00","id":1374375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1369314#post1369314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe someone here on the forums still has a copy of the fixed version.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do.<br /> <br /> Please PM me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Oh, what is your web-address? I would like to read more of your stuff.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T14:35:36-07:00","id":1374978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1369304#post1369304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can these still be found online by the way? Assuming it was a free pdf i mean</div> </div> </div> </div>It's now available again for download at <a href=\"http://personal.jargon-file.org/Annals%20of%20Inherited%20Might.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://personal.jargon-file.org/Anna...ed%20Might.pdf</a> thanks to Daredevil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T08:22:16-07:00","id":1375084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible?p=1366968#post1366968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cause i sure as hell did not see any such thing in scrolls of errata or ink monkeys.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Charm <i>Should the Sun Not Rise </i>in <b>Glories of the Most High</b> and the entire &quot;errata&quot; creation of Magnanimous Unbound Sun were direct edit-war responses to things other freelancers were doing.<br /> <br /> Nowadays, things are much more centralized - that sort of thing wouldn't happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 03-16-2020, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T09:15:39-07:00","id":1375096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365243-why-is-resurrection-impossible#post1365243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a related note, reincarnation itself IS a resurrection of sorts. It's even possible for a hun to remember some things from the life right before this one. In theory you could store someone's memories, trace his reincarnation and give them back to him. Depending on how much &quot;mojo&quot; you have, you may be able to recreate them just like that with whatever metaphysical explanation you can come with for your spell/artifact/etc</div> </div> </div> </div>Remembering past lives perfectly is the province of Artifact N/As, like Domnica's Mantle. Certain characteristics may carry across successive reincarnations of the hun, but memories are largely wiped by the mechanism of Lethe and the Well of Souls, which are currently the only way to successfully reintegrate the two halves of the human soul. Other methods have <i>significant </i>drawbacks, up to someone countermagicing your sorcerous android and &quot;killing&quot; it, or a Liminal destroying the Frankenstein you've made because that's how they roll. There's just no free lunch.<br /> <br /> You say that the out of game reason is obvious, but it's worth definitively re-stating: <b>Exalted </b>is a game with consequences to your actions. You can't undo what has been done, you can only create something anew. For myself, I find stories with consequences to be frankly more interesting than stories that aren't; instead of making the story about the success of resurrection, it's more interesting to wonder: what did the character <i>do </i>that they want to undo so very badly, and why? Why do they fear death so much that they seek immortality, and what ruin do they leave in their wake?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 03-16-2020, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T19:56:42-07:00","id":1377443,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me to flip the question around. Why <i>should</i> resurrection be possible? Why should one have to justify that death is a permanent thing?<br /> <br /> I get that in many games and other media, once characters reach a certain level of power, death is treated more like a status effect than a narrative event. And Exalted are very powerful, sure, and can do many miraculous things. But does that mean the universe isn't allowed to say that some things are beyond even miracles, because that's just how things are? That death is <i>an ending</i>, not a pause, and that true resurrection is as patently nonsensical as reaching the top of a mountain and then climbing some more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 03-30-2020, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T11:18:52-07:00","id":1377538,"title":"","content":"I always liked to think that Resurrection being impossible was the doing of the Exalted. Back in the day Ruvelia, one of the twin hearts of the King of the Titans, had power over resurrection. She was killed in the early days of the Primordial War by an Exalted Host who feared the disastrous consequences of her power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}